"pulse_sheet_about_title" = "About pulse";
"pulse_sheet_about_body" = "Pulse is the number of heartbeats per minute (bpm).\n\nTamyrFlow shows pulse data from compatible connected devices or Apple Health with your permission.\n\nValues may change with activity, rest, and other factors.\n\nTamyrFlow is for tracking activity and general wellness. It is not intended for diagnosis, treatment, or medical monitoring. If you have health questions, consult a professional.";
"pulse_sheet_how_title" = "How TamyrFlow gets pulse";
"pulse_sheet_how_body" = "TamyrFlow does not measure pulse with the phone itself.\n\nIf you have a compatible watch, connect it in My Watch. When the device sends pulse readings, they can appear in the app.\n\nYou can also allow access to pulse data in Apple Health.\n\nAfter tapping Update data, TamyrFlow requests available new records and refreshes history, charts, and stats.\n\nIf there are no new measurements, previously saved values remain.\n\nPermissions and available measurements are required to show indicators.";
"pulse_sheet_problems_title" = "Update problems";
"pulse_sheet_problems_body" = "If data is not updating:\n\nCheck that Bluetooth is on.\nMake sure the watch is connected and nearby.\nCheck Health data permissions.\nConfirm the watch has pulse measurements.\nTry updating again.\n\nIf the problem continues, open Support.";
"pulse_sheet_zones_title" = "Pulse zones";
"pulse_sheet_zones_body" = "Pulse zones help estimate activity intensity.\n\n• Rest — rest and low activity.\n• Light — light activity.\n• Moderate — moderate intensity.\n• High — high-intensity effort.\n\nDuration and share of time in each zone are based on available measurements and configured thresholds.\n\nZones are for fitness analytics and are not a medical assessment.";
